\section{Depth Extrapolation}
\label{app:depth}

Figure~\ref{fig:depth} resolves the S1 and S2 columns of
Table~\ref{tab:main-results} by depth; each column is the count-weighted mean
of its depths. Training caps the reached state at
\(80\) tokens, so depths \(128\)--\(512\) are pure extrapolation. Deeper states
are rarer, so the number of available test states per seed falls from
\(1{,}000\) at depth \(5\) to \(963\) at \(80\), \(908\) at \(128\), \(711\) at
\(256\), and \(462\) at \(512\). \method{} holds the lowest attack success at
every one of the eight depths. Its absolute margin over Base neither grows nor
collapses outside the trained range---\(38.8\)~pp at depth \(5\),
\(38.0\)~pp at \(128\), and \(35.9\)~pp at \(512\)---but the relative
reduction does narrow, from \(67\)\% at depth \(5\) to \(48\)\% at \(512\),
because Base itself degrades fastest at the deepest states.

