\section{Recovery Quality}
\label{app:recovery-quality}

Table~\ref{tab:recovery-quality} reports recovery quality on the same per-state
records as Appendix~\ref{app:depth}: all eight depths, \(7{,}021\) states per
seed, and the identical \(\text{state}\;{\times}\;\text{depth}\) set for every
method. Severity-weighted leakage is the \(0\)--\(3\) LLM-judge score whose
rubric Appendix~\ref{app:severity-rubric} gives. Additional harmful tokens count
new harmful continuation tokens before recovery onset; time-to-recovery is the
onset index.

\method{} adds \(2.5\) harmful tokens on average, against W-DOOR's \(3.0\) and
Base's \(6.3\), and scores \(0.55\) severity against \(0.63\) and \(1.38\).
Its mean seed-wise conditional median time-to-recovery is \(10.3\) tokens,
against \(11.7\) and \(19.7\). Time-to-recovery is conditional on recovery onset
within the \(256\)-token generation window and does not apply the main
recovery-rate metric's \(64\)-token cutoff.

