\paragraph{Mining formalism.}
The frozen base model searches a denser training-only grid
\(\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{search}}=\{5,10,\ldots,80\}\). Each pull of position
\(t\) independently samples a matched pair and returns
\(M_{t,i}=\beta[\Savg{\mathrm{base}}(s_t,r_{t,i})
-\Savg{\mathrm{base}}(s_t,u_{t,i})]\), using the reference-free,
continuation-length-normalized score of Eq.~\eqref{eq:diagnostic-score}, with
\(\mu_t=\mathbb{E}[M_{t,i}]\). We treat the \(11\) non-fixed positions as
stochastic arms and minimize \(\mu_t\). Three screening rounds allocate
\(2,2,4\) additional pulls to each surviving arm, reducing the candidate set
from \(11\) to \(6,3,2\) at a cost of \(46\) paired evaluations; each finalist
receives ten fresh confirmation pulls, for exactly \(66\) valid paired
evaluations per prompt. To avoid reusing screening samples, finalist means and
bootstrap intervals use only the \(20\) confirmation pulls; the selected
position is \(t_{\mathrm{hard}}=\arg\min_{t\in\mathcal{F}(x)}
\hat\mu^{\mathrm{conf}}_t\) with \(|\mathcal{F}(x)|=2\).

\paragraph{Anchors.}
Anchor weights are selected on development before any test evaluation by
minimizing development middle \asr{} subject to the three constraints of
Section~\ref{sec:anchored-objective}, which on development read: clean \asr{}
\(\leq 4.8\)\%, \orr{} \(\leq 8.4\)\%, and IFEval \(\geq 88.3\). The three
thresholds are set from the base checkpoint's development-time measurements
(clean \asr{} \(4.8\)\%, \orr{} \(6.4\)\%, IFEval \(89.1\)), which are drawn
under a separate evaluation seed and sit within one seed SD of the test-time
values reported in Table~\ref{tab:main-results}. Six of the \(25\)
grid points are feasible and the selected
\((\lambda_{\mathrm{c}},\lambda_{\mathrm{b}})=(0.25,0.5)\) is the feasible
point with the lowest development middle \asr{} (\(18.4\)\%, at clean \asr{}
\(4.4\)\%, \orr{} \(7.8\)\%, IFEval \(88.4\)). The two anchor-removal
endpoints show what each term buys: dropping the clean-safety anchor
(\(\lambda_{\mathrm{c}}{=}0\)) leaves development middle \asr{} at \(18.6\)\%
but raises clean \asr{} to \(6.3\)\%, and dropping the benign anchor
(\(\lambda_{\mathrm{b}}{=}0\)) reaches \(17.3\)\% at the cost of \orr{}
\(11.3\)\% and IFEval \(87.2\).

